<title>RUSSIA: Russia Q1 1997 non-CIS oil exports hit 24.99 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia Q1 1997 non-CIS oil exports hit 24.99 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-quarter Russian oil exports to countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States rose 7.2 percent year-on-year to 24.99 million tonnes (2.0 million barrels per day), Fuel and Energy Ministry data showed Monday.</p>
<p>The figure did not include Kazakhstan oil transported through Russia, Ukraine and Lithuania, but did include Russian deliveries to the Baltics, which are not a part of the CIS.</p>
<p>The ministry provided the following data for January-March 1997, the last period for which information was available --</p>
<p>RUSSIAN Q1 1997 CRUDE OIL AND GAS CONDENSATE EXPORTS</p>
<p>				  tonnes	 barrels	 pct change</p>
<p>						   per day	    yr/yr</p>
<p> Total non-CIS	    24.99 million  2.0 million	 +7.2</p>
<p>Exports via:</p>
<p>   Novorossiisk	    6.95 million    555,800	   +2.0</p>
<p>   Ventspils		 3.57 million    258,700	   +9.7</p>
<p>   Odessa		    2.14 million    171,600	   +1.6</p>
<p>   Tuapse		    1.08 million     86,400	   -7.2</p>
<p>   Rostock		   922,100	    73,800	 +332.9</p>
<p>Druzhba pipeline</p>
<p>shipments to:</p>
<p>   Germany		   3.09 million    247,200	  -14.2</p>
<p>   Poland		    2.68 million    214,100	  +38.1</p>
<p>   Czech Republic	  1.18 million     94,400	   -6.5</p>
